        <register>
        <name>IFCR5</name>
          <description>There is an Identifier Filter Control Register (IFCRn) for each filter. \newline Even-numbered instances of IFCRn (IFCR0, IFCR2, IFCR4, and so on) act as filters in both identifier list and identifier mask modes. \newline Odd-numbered instances of IFCRn (IFCR1, IFCR3, IFCR5, and so on) act as: \begin{itemize}[] \item Filters in identifier list mode. \item A mask for the preceding-numbered register in identifier mask mode. For example, if filters 0 and 1 are configured for identifier mask mode, IFCR1 acts as a mask for IFCR0. \end{itemize} The IFCRn registers are read-only in Normal mode and can be written only in Initialization mode.</description>
